description.narrative:
The overall objective of the contribution EBRD SWUK 2 - Ukraine Municipal Infrastructure Cooperation Account 2020-2025 is to promote necessary reforms and support critical infrastructure investments in the municipal sector of Ukraine by providing the EBRD with access to the dedicated grant funding for technical cooperation assignments. 

Technical cooperation assignments will help the clients of the EBRD, Ukrainian municipalities, to improve capacity of their utility companies, regional authorities for project implementation and follow-up, ensure compliance with stricter environmental and social standards, and provide assistance with targeted reforms. This will empower Ukrainian municipalities to work on investment projects in critical municipal infrastructure with the EBRD using financial structures and instruments, aiming at:

- EU-integration;
- Reduced emissions to the environment;
- Sustainable use of natural resources;
- Sustainable public services;
- Energy efficiency;
- Institutional reforms and sustainability of services; and
- Transition and social inclusion;

The projects will be in compliance with EBRDs policies, rules and procedures and support the objectives of the results strategy for Swedens reform cooperation.


SWUK 2 remains relevant under the new Strategy for Swedens reconstruction and reform cooperation with Ukraine 20232027 (approved July 2023). SWUK 2 builds upon the EBRD SWUK 1 - Energy Efficiency and Environment Cooperation Fund 2009-2026 (53060018) and is complementary to 55030134 E5P Eastern Europe Energy Efficiency and Environment Partnership  Regional.

Swedish support to critical element of the project cycle will enable EBRD to provide funding for important social, environment and climate investment projects that will act as a catalyst for sectoral reforms, provide measurable results in terms of decreased environmental pollution rates, increase sustainability of public services in areas such as district heating, water and sewage, waste management, energy efficiency and renewable energy, public transport, contribute to the climate change mitigation and adaptation efforts.
